<article class="env-definition" id="016W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/016W">Definition <span data-tag="016W">14.8.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $U, V, W$ be simplicial objects of $\mathcal{C}$. Let $a : U \to V$, $b : U \to W$ be morphisms. Assume the pushouts $V_ n \amalg _{U_ n} W_ n$ exist in $\mathcal{C}$. The <em>pushout of $V$ and $W$ over $U$</em> is the simplicial object $V\amalg _ U W$ defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$(V \amalg _ U W)_ n = V_ n \amalg _{U_ n} W_ n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$d^ n_ i = (d^ n_ i, d^ n_ i)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$s^ n_ i = (s^ n_ i, s^ n_ i)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In other words, $V\amalg _ U W$ is the pushout of the presheaves $V$ and $W$ over the presheaf $U$ on $\Delta $. </p>
</article>